Hello,<br><br>I have ordered a new TYT MD-9600 without GPS from this dealer:<br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-505.html" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-505.html</a><br><br>OpenGD77 Firmware "MD9600_firmware_V5HW.zip" flashed.<br>Device works perfectly.<br><br>The squelch can be set in "FM" mode using the arrow keys. The squelch closes.<br>However, you can still hear a low noise in the loudspeaker when the squelch is closed.<br>In "DMR" mode, you can also hear a slight hiss, but a little less than in FM!<br><br>I have a second MD-9600 and when the squelch is closed there is absolutely no noise in the loudspeaker!<br><br>Can anyone here give me a tip on how to eliminate the low noise when the squelch is closed?<br><br>Thank you, Alfred OE7ABH<br><a href="https://tyrofly.at/funk.htm#Digitalfunk" class="postlink">https://tyrofly.at/funk.htm#Digitalfunk</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1060">oe7abh</a> — Wed Mar 26, 2025 1:02 pm</p><hr />
